Explore the imposing <strong>Agra Fort</strong>, North India&#39;s premier red sandstone fortification, erected by Mughal Emperor Akbar in 1565. The fort&#39;s royal audience halls, expansive stone courtyards, elegant marble mosque, and private royal chambers provide a window into the Mughal Empire&#39;s brilliance in blending defensive architecture with aesthetic finesse.<br />
<br />
