                                            [city_id] => 8
                                            [description] => <ul>
	<li><u>Discovering Agra&#39;s Treasures: Mehtab Bagh, Agra Fort, and Fatehpur Sikri</u></li>
</ul>
<p>Begin your day at the enchanting <strong>Mehtab Bagh</strong>, a Mughal garden across the Taj Mahal, beyond the Yamuna River. Revel in a stroll while admiring the captivating view of the Taj Mahal from afar.
<br />
Explore the imposing <strong>Agra Fort</strong>, North India&#39;s premier red sandstone fortification, erected by Mughal Emperor Akbar in 1565. The fort&#39;s royal audience halls, expansive stone courtyards, elegant marble mosque, and private royal chambers provide a window into the Mughal Empire&#39;s brilliance in blending defensive architecture with aesthetic finesse.<br />
<br />
Departure to your next destination, and En-route, visit the mysterious <strong>Fatehpur Sikri</strong>, a deserted city that stands as one of the world&#39;s most impeccably preserved ghost cities. A testament to Emperor Akbar&#39;s visionary rule, this architectural marvel was constructed in 1571, harmoniously merging Persian court styles with prevailing Hindu-Islamic influences. The city&#39;s original red sandstone edifices remain as exquisite as when they were first sculpted. Among the numerous wonders is the Diwan I Khas&#39; Jewel House, a unique single-storey structure featuring four doorways and an intricately carved central pillar that supports a seat accessible via suspended walkways.</p>

                                        )

                                )

                        )

