                    [events] => Array
                        (
                            [0] => Array
                                (
                                    [id] => 323
                                    [name] => N-207 - 2 Day - Agra (D1 - Arr.Sur+Taj+Fort | D2 - Mehtab+Sikri)
                                    [event_id] => 207
                                    [description] => <p>Day 1 &ndash; Journey to the City of Love: Agra<br /><br />Begin your journey with a comfortable drive to Agra, the romantic city that once served as the illustrious capital of the Mughal Empire during the 16th and 17th centuries. Agra is home to three magnificent UNESCO World Heritage Sites&mdash;the Taj Mahal, Agra Fort, and Fatehpur Sikri&mdash;each echoing stories of imperial grandeur and timeless love.<br /><br />Afternoon: Agra Fort &amp; Taj Mahal<br /><br />Explore the majestic Agra Fort (Lal Qila), a massive red sandstone fortress commissioned by Emperor Akbar. This UNESCO World Heritage Site symbolizes Mughal power, resilience, and architectural brilliance. Wander through its splendid palaces, mosques, and audience halls, including Macchi Bhawan, Shah Jahani Mahal, Khas Mahal, Mina Masjid, Nagina Masjid, and the impressive Diwan-i-Am (Hall of Public Audience).<br /><br />Later, enjoy a charming horse-drawn carriage ride to the iconic Taj Mahal, one of the Seven Wonders of the World. Built by Emperor Shah Jahan in loving memory of his queen Mumtaz Mahal, this 17th-century white marble masterpiece mesmerizes with its perfect symmetry, serene gardens, royal gateways, and exquisite craftsmanship.<br /><br />Included (Day 1):<br />Monument entrance fees &bull; Decorated horse-carriage / battery-van ride &bull; Personal English-speaking guide &bull; Private chauffeur-driven vehicle<br /><br />Day 2 &ndash; Sunrise Serenity &amp; Imperial Legacy<br />Morning: Mehtab Bagh &ndash; Sunrise View of the Taj Mahal<br /><br />Witness the magical sunrise view of the Taj Mahal from Mehtab Bagh, a beautifully laid Mughal garden located across the Yamuna River. As the first rays of the sun illuminate the marble fa&ccedil;ade, enjoy a tranquil and less-crowded perspective of this eternal monument.<br /><br />Included:<br />Monument entrance fees &bull; Battery-van ride &bull; Personal English-speaking guide &bull; Private chauffeur-driven vehicle<br /><br />En-Route: Fatehpur Sikri &ndash; The Abandoned Mughal Capital<br /><br />Continue your journey with a visit to Fatehpur Sikri, the magnificent yet deserted Mughal city and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Once the capital of Emperor Akbar, this architectural marvel captivates visitors with its remarkably preserved palaces, courtyards, and religious structures.<br /><br />Explore iconic landmarks such as Jama Masjid, Buland Darwaza, Tomb of Salim Chishti, Ibadat Khana, Mariam-us-Zamani&rsquo;s Palace, Naubat Khana, Birbal&rsquo;s House, and the elegant Panch Mahal, each reflecting the artistic and cultural zenith of the Mughal era.<br /><br />Included:<br />Monument entrance fees &bull; Battery-van ride &bull; Personal English-speaking guide &bull; Private chauffeur-driven vehicle</p>
                                )

