<p><em><strong>New Delhi </strong>is the capital of India, has been  inhabited continuously since the 6th century BCE and has served as the  capital of multiple kingdoms and empires throughout its history. In the  1920s, it was redesigned by Sir Edwin Lutyens and Sir Herbert Baker.  Today, Delhi is a bustling metropolis that serves as a vibrant hub of  international arts and culture and a thriving commercial centre.</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Please note that the standard check-in time at hotels is 2 pm. As  most  international flights arrive in the evening or night, we do not  have any  sightseeing activities planned for the first day of the trip.  However,  if your flight arrives early in the day and you don\'t require  time to  recuperate from international travel, we can arrange some  sightseeing on  the first day of the trip at an additional charge.</p>
